# Deny by default, then name what the image needs. An allow-list is the only
# form of this file that cannot leak a new secret the day someone adds one:
# with a deny-list, `config/paper.env` is safe and the next credential file is
# not.
*

!requirements.txt
!src/**
!scripts/**

# Read by scripts/test_stops_table_coverage.py, which the image runs.
!README.md

# Even inside what is allowed, never the caches or local state.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.env
